             \u2502\n\u2502  The previous error regarding ASCII art in `outputs.tf` has been resolved    \u2502\n\u2502  by implementing standard HCL output blocks. Dependency chains between       \u2502\n\u2502  modules (Networking -> Security/Compute) have been properly established     \u2502\n\u2502  via input variables.                                                        \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2570\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256f\n\n\u256d\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 \ud83d\udccb Task Completion \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256e\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Task Completed                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Name: Based on the Architect's modular design, implement the Terraform      \u2502\n\u2502  project: aws-single-node-compute-stack.                                     \u2502\n\u2502  --- ARCHITECTURE DESIGN ---                                                 \u2502\n\u2502  PROJECT_SLUG: aws-single-node-compute-stack                                 \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 1. Provider and Resource Mapping                                        \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Provider:** `hashicorp/aws`                                           \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Networking:** VPC, Public Subnet, Internet Gateway, Route Table.      \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Compute:** EC2 Instance (t3.xlarge), EBS Volume (50GB).               \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Security:** Security Group (SSH access), TLS Private Key (for PEM     \u2502\n\u2502  file).                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Identity:** IAM Instance Profile (optional, if needed for role-based  \u2502\n\u2502  access).                                                                    \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 2. Modular Architecture Layout                                          \u2502\n\u2502  ```text                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502  .                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500\u2500 main.tf                 # Root module calling submodules                \u2502\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500\u2500 providers.tf            # Provider configuration                        \u2502\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500\u2500 modules/                                                                \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 networking/         # VPC, Subnet, IGW, Route Table                 \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 security/           # Security Group, TLS Key Pair                  \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 compute/            # EC2 Instance, EBS Volume                      \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 3. Implementation Details                                               \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  **providers.tf**                                                            \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  terraform {                                                                 \u2502\n\u2502    required_providers {                                                      \u2502\n\u2502      aws = { source = \"hashicorp/aws\", version = \"~> 5.0\" }                  \u2502\n\u2502      tls = { source = \"hashicorp/tls\", version = \"~> 4.0\" }                  \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  provider \"aws\" { region = \"us-east-1\" }                                     \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  **modules/networking/main.tf**                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Creates a basic VPC and a single Public Subnet with an Internet Gateway     \u2502\n\u2502  for external connectivity.                                                  \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  **modules/security/main.tf**                                                \u2502\n\u2502  Generates an `tls_private_key` to create an `aws_key_pair` and defines an   \u2502\n\u2502  `aws_security_group` allowing port 22.                                      \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  **modules/compute/main.tf**                                                 \u2502\n\u2502  Provisions the `aws_instance` (t3.xlarge) and attaches an `aws_ebs_volume`  \u2502\n\u2502  (50GB).                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 4. Cloud Infrastructure Topology                                        \u2502\n\u2502  ```mermaid                                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  graph TD                                                                    \u2502\n\u2502      Internet((Internet)) --> IGW[Internet Gateway]                          \u2502\n\u2502      IGW --> RT[Route Table]                                                 \u2502\n\u2502      RT --> Subnet[Public Subnet]                                            \u2502\n\u2502      Subnet --> SG[Security Group: Port 22]                                  \u2502\n\u2502      SG --> EC2[EC2 Instance: t3.xlarge]                                     \u2502\n\u2502      EC2 --> EBS[(EBS Volume: 50GB)]                                         \u2502\n\u2502      User((Client)) -- SSH Access --> EC2                                    \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 5. Root Module (main.tf)                                                \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  module \"networking\" {                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    source = \"./modules/networking\"                                           \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  module \"security\" {                                                         \u2502\n\u2502    source = \"./modules/security\"                                             \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  module \"compute\" {                                                          \u2502\n\u2502    source        = \"./modules/compute\"                                       \u2502\n\u2502    vpc_id        = module.networking.vpc_id                                  \u2502\n\u2502    subnet_id     = module.networking.public_subnet_id                        \u2502\n\u2502    key_name      = module.security.key_name                                  \u2502\n\u2502    sec_group_id  = module.security.security_group_id                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  **Summary of Resource Roles:**                                              \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Networking Module:** Establishes the network boundary and path to     \u2502\n\u2502  the internet.                                                               \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Security Module:** Manages the cryptographic identity (PEM key) and   \u2502\n\u2502  firewall rules (Security Group).                                            \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Compute Module:** Orchestrates the deployment of the t3.xlarge        \u2502\n\u2502  instance and storage attachment.                                            \u2502\n\u2502  ---------------------------                                                 \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  \u26a0\ufe0f--- ATTENTION: PREVIOUS ROUND FAILED ---                                  \u2502\n\u2502  Please correct the following errors and apply this advice in the new        \u2502\n\u2502  configuration:                                                              \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  \ud83d\udd2c Dynamic Reflection Debugging Analysis:                                   \u2502\n\u2502    - Cause of Error: The file 'outputs.tf' contains a file-system directory  \u2502\n\u2502  tree structure (ASCII art) instead of valid Terraform HCL code. Terraform   \u2502\n\u2502  is attempting to parse these characters as language syntax, which results   \u2502\n\u2502  in 'Invalid character' and 'Argument or block definition required' errors.  \u2502\n\u2502    - Fix Instructions: Remove the directory tree diagram from 'outputs.tf'.  \u2502\n\u2502  If you intend to export values from your root module, replace the content   \u2502\n\u2502  with valid 'output' blocks that reference the outputs from your child       \u2502\n\u2502  modules.                                                                    \u2502\n\u2502    - Correct HCL Template Snippet:                                           \u2502\n\u2502  output \"vpc_id\" {                                                           \u2502\n\u2502    value = module.networking.vpc_id                                          \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  output \"public_ip\" {                                                        \u2502\n\u2502    value = module.compute.public_ip                                          \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  output \"security_group_id\" {                                                \u2502\n\u2502    value = module.security.security_group_id                                 \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  -------------------------------------------                                 \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## MANDATORY RULES (FAILURE TO FOLLOW = BROKEN CODE)                        \u2502\n\u2502  1. You MUST use the `Write Terraform File` tool for EVERY SINGLE FILE you   \u2502\n\u2502  create.                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502  2. DO NOT WRITE PLAIN TEXT TERRAFORM. YOU MUST CALL THE TOOL.               \u2502\n\u2502  3. If you need to create 15 files, you MUST call the tool 15 times.         \u2502\n\u2502  4. If a \"PREVIOUS ROUND FAILED\" block is present, you MUST prioritize       \u2502\n\u2502  correcting the reported errors and applying the provided KNOWN FIX          \u2502\n\u2502  GUIDANCE or reflection advice. You MUST override the Architect design if    \u2502\n\u2502  it contradicts the required fix (e.g. if the design specifies               \u2502\n\u2502  \"enable_auto_scaling = true\" but the guidance instructs to rename it to     \u2502\n\u2502  \"auto_scaling_enabled = true\", you MUST apply the rename).                  \u2502\n\u2502  5. STRICT MODULAR STRUCTURE REQUIREMENT:                                    \u2502\n\u2502     You MUST organize the code into logical submodules under the `modules/`  \u2502\n\u2502  directory (e.g., `./modules/networking`, `./modules/aks`,                   \u2502\n\u2502  `./modules/acr`).                                                           \u2502\n\u2502     The root `main.tf` must only call these modules. You MUST use the        \u2502\n\u2502  `Write Terraform File` tool to create `main.tf`, `variables.tf`, and        \u2502\n\u2502  `outputs.tf` for EACH module, as well as the root files.                    \u2502\n\u2502     DO NOT write all resources flatly in the root directory.                 \u2502\n\u2502  6. You MUST create a `README.md` in the project ROOT.                       \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## HCL FORMATTING (CRITICAL)                                                \u2502\n\u2502  - NEVER use semicolons (;) to separate arguments. Use NEWLINES.             \u2502\n\u2502  - Every resource argument MUST be on its own line.                          \u2502\n\u2502  - Every closing brace } MUST be on its own line.                            \u2502\n\u2502  - BAD:  resource \"aws_subnet\" \"s1\" { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id; cidr_block   \u2502\n\u2502  = \"10.0.1.0/24\" }                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  - GOOD:                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502    resource \"aws_subnet\" \"s1\" {                                              \u2502\n\u2502      vpc_id     = aws_vpc.main.id                                            \u2502\n\u2502      cidr_block = \"10.0.1.0/24\"                                              \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## REQUIRED FILES                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  - Root files: Define the `terraform { required_providers { } }` block and   \u2502\n\u2502  `provider` block exactly once in `versions.tf` or root `main.tf`. DO NOT    \u2502\n\u2502  duplicate provider blocks in submodules.                                    \u2502\n\u2502  - Root `variables.tf`: Input variables (e.g., region).                      \u2502\n\u2502  - Root `outputs.tf`: Key outputs (endpoints, IDs, ARNs).                    \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## EKS / INFRASTRUCTURE COMPLETENESS CHECKLIST                              \u2502\n\u2502  If creating EKS, you MUST include ALL of the following:                     \u2502\n\u2502  - At least 2 subnets across 2 different Availability Zones (EKS requires    \u2502\n\u2502  this).                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  - Subnets must have `map_public_ip_on_launch = true` for public clusters.   \u2502\n\u2502  - IAM roles MUST have `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` resources:           \u2502\n\u2502    * Cluster role: AmazonEKSClusterPolicy                                    \u2502\n\u2502    * Node role: AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy,                                   \u2502\n\u2502  AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryReadOnly, AmazonEKS_CNI_Policy                    \u2502\n\u2502  - EKS `vpc_config` must include `endpoint_public_access = true` for public  \u2502\n\u2502  clusters.                                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  - Node group must have `depends_on` referencing the IAM policy              \u2502\n\u2502  attachments.                                                                \u2502\n\u2502  - Subnets should be tagged: `kubernetes.io/cluster/<name> = shared`.        \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Project Slug: aws-single-node-compute-stack                                 \u2502\n\u2502  Agent: Senior Terraform Developer                                           \u2502\n\u