urce`                           \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Location:** `modules/security/outputs.tf`                             \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Details:** The output `key_name` attempts to reference                \u2502\n\u2502  `aws_key_pair.generated_key`, but this resource is not defined within the   \u2502\n\u2502  `modules/security/` module.                                                 \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Required Action:** Ensure that the resource name defined in           \u2502\n\u2502  `modules/security/main.tf` matches the reference in                         \u2502\n\u2502  `modules/security/outputs.tf`. If the resource is named differently,        \u2502\n\u2502  update the output block accordingly.                                        \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  #### 2. Security Review Findings                                            \u2502\n\u2502  While the syntax error prevents full deployment, a preliminary security     \u2502\n\u2502  review of the architectural design indicates the following requirements     \u2502\n\u2502  for your next iteration:                                                    \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Security Groups:** Ensure that the Security Group in                  \u2502\n\u2502  `modules/security/` follows the Principle of Least Privilege.               \u2502\n\u2502  Specifically, verify that SSH (port 22) access is restricted to a specific  \u2502\n\u2502  CIDR range (e.g., your office/VPN IP) rather than `0.0.0.0/0`.              \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Encryption at Rest:** Ensure the 50GB EBS volume defined in           \u2502\n\u2502  `modules/compute/` has the `encrypted = true` attribute set.                \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Instance Metadata:** Verify that the EC2 instance is configured to    \u2502\n\u2502  use IMDSv2 (Instance